=== lvcreate ===
USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  lvcreate -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate -i|--stripes Number -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate -m|--mirrors Number -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate --type raid -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate -m|--mirrors Number -i|--stripes Number -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate -s|--snapshot -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] LV
  lvcreate --type thin-pool -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate --type cache-pool -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate -V|--virtualsize Size[m|UNIT] --thinpool LV VG
  lvcreate -s|--snapshot LV
  lvcreate --type thin --thinpool LV LV
  lvcreate --type vdo -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] VG
  lvcreate --type cache -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] --cachepool LV VG
  lvcreate --type cache -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] --cachevol LV VG
  lvcreate --type cache -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] --cachedevice PV VG
  lvcreate --type writecache -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] --cachevol LV VG
  lvcreate --type writecache -L|--size Size[m|UNIT] --cachedevice PV VG


FLAGS (156) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Create a linear LV
-L, --size Size[m|UNIT]
    --type linear
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]

Create a striped LV ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    --type striped
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]

Create a raid1 or mirror LV ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    --type
                                 values: raid1, mirror
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-R, --regionsize Size[m|UNIT]
    --mirrorlog
                                 values: core, disk
    --minrecoveryrate Size[k|UNIT]
    --maxrecoveryrate Size[k|UNIT]

Create a raid LV (a specific raid level must be used, e.g. raid1) ──────────
    --type raid
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-m, --mirrors Number
-R, --regionsize Size[m|UNIT]
    --minrecoveryrate Size[k|UNIT]
    --maxrecoveryrate Size[k|UNIT]
    --raidintegrity
                                 values: y, n
    --raidintegritymode String
    --raidintegrityblocksize Number

Create a raid10 LV ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    --type raid10
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-R, --regionsize Size[m|UNIT]
    --minrecoveryrate Size[k|UNIT]
    --maxrecoveryrate Size[k|UNIT]

Create a COW snapshot LV of an origin LV ───────────────────────────────────
    --type snapshot
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-c, --chunksize Size[k|UNIT]

Create a thin pool ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    --type thin-pool
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-T, --thin
-c, --chunksize Size[k|UNIT]
    --thinpool LV_new
    --discards
                                 values: passdown, nopassdown, ignore
    --errorwhenfull
                                 values: y, n
    --poolmetadatasize Size[m|UNIT]
    --poolmetadataspare
                                 values: y, n

Create a cache pool ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    --type cache-pool
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-H, --cache
-c, --chunksize Size[k|UNIT]
    --cachemode
                                 values: writethrough, writeback,
                                 passthrough
    --cachepolicy String
    --cachesettings String
    --cachemetadataformat
                                 values: auto, 1, 2
    --poolmetadatasize Size[m|UNIT]
    --poolmetadataspare
                                 values: y, n

Create a thin LV in a thin pool ────────────────────────────────────────────
    --type thin
-T, --thin

Create a thin LV that is a snapshot of an existing thin LV ─────────────────
-s, --snapshot LV
    --type thin

Create a thin LV that is a snapshot of an external origin LV ───────────────
    --type thin
-T, --thin

Create a LV that returns VDO when used ─────────────────────────────────────
    --type vdo
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-V, --virtualsize Size[m|UNIT]
    --vdo
    --vdopool LV_new
    --compression
                                 values: y, n
    --deduplication
                                 values: y, n
    --vdosettings String

Create a new LV, then attach the specified cachepool which converts the new
LV to type cache
    --type cache
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-H, --cache
-c, --chunksize Size[k|UNIT]
    --cachemode
                                 values: writethrough, writeback,
                                 passthrough
    --cachepolicy String
    --cachesettings String
    --cachemetadataformat
                                 values: auto, 1, 2
    --poolmetadatasize Size[m|UNIT]
    --poolmetadataspare
                                 values: y, n

Create a new LV, then attach the specified cachevol which converts the new
LV to type cache
    --type cache
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-c, --chunksize Size[k|UNIT]
    --cachemode
                                 values: writethrough, writeback,
                                 passthrough
    --cachepolicy String
    --cachesettings String
    --cachemetadataformat
                                 values: auto, 1, 2

Create a new LV, then attach a cachevol created from the specified cache
device, which converts the new LV to type cache
    --type cache
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
-c, --chunksize Size[k|UNIT]
    --cachesize Size[m|UNIT]
    --cachemode
                                 values: writethrough, writeback,
                                 passthrough
    --cachepolicy String
    --cachesettings String
    --cachemetadataformat
                                 values: auto, 1, 2

Create a new LV, then attach the specified cachevol which converts the new
LV to type writecache
    --type writecache
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
    --cachesettings String

Create a new LV, then attach a cachevol created from the specified cache
device, which converts the new LV to type writecache
    --type writecache
-l, --extents Number[PERCENT]
-i, --stripes Number
-I, --stripesize Size[k|UNIT]
    --cachesize Size[m|UNIT]
    --cachesettings String

Common options for command ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
-a, --activate
                                 values: y, n, ay
-A, --autobackup
                                 values: y, n
-C, --contiguous
                                 values: y, n
-M, --persistent
                                 values: y, n
-j, --major Number
-k, --setactivationskip
                                 values: y, n
-K, --ignoreactivationskip
-n, --name String
-p, --permission
                                 values: rw, r
-r, --readahead
                                 values: auto, none, Number
-W, --wipesignatures
                                 values: y, n
-Z, --zero
                                 values: y, n
    --addtag Tag
    --alloc
                                 values: contiguous, cling, cling_by_tags,
                                 normal, anywhere, inherit
    --setautoactivation
                                 values: y, n
    --ignoremonitoring
    --metadataprofile String
    --minor Number
    --monitor
                                 values: y, n
    --nosync
    --noudevsync
    --reportformat
                                 values: basic, json

Common options for lvm ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-d, --debug
-h, --help
-q, --quiet
-v, --verbose
-y, --yes
-t, --test
    --commandprofile String
    --config String
    --driverloaded
                                 values: y, n
    --nolocking
    --lockopt String
    --longhelp
    --profile String
    --version
    --devicesfile String
    --devices PV
    --nohints
    --journal String
